-- title:
--   Carayol's lemma: lifts descend to their trace subalgebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a finite index type $n$, a topological group $G$, and a commutative local ring $\mathcal O$ with finite residue field $k =$ `ResidueField 𝓞`. Let $A$ be an object of [`Deformation.ProartinianCat 𝓞`](def/Deformations_ProartinianCat.html#L44), that is, a topological local $\mathcal O$-algebra which is pro-Artinian, whose structure map is a local homomorphism and which has residue field $k$. Let $\rho_0 \colon G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(k)$ be a continuous monoid homomorphism (the structure map of $A$ onto $k$ being the unique morphism to the terminal object `ProartinianCat.residueField`), and assume the associated representation of $G$ on $n \to k$ is absolutely irreducible, in the sense that for every field $k'$ with a $k$-algebra structure the base change $k' \otimes \rho_0$ is irreducible. Let $\rho' \colon G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(A)$ be a continuous monoid homomorphism lying in the subfunctor `liftFunctor n G 𝓞 ρ₀` at $A$, i.e. whose reduction along $A \to k$ is exactly $\rho_0$. Then `TraceAlgebra.Descends ρ'` holds: there is a $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_n(A)$, acting by conjugation and lying in the kernel of $\mathrm{GL}_n(A) \to \mathrm{GL}_n(k)$, such that for every $g \in G$ and all indices $i, j$ the $(i,j)$ entry of $\gamma \rho'(g) \gamma^{-1}$ lies in the topological closure of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $A$ generated by the set `traceSet 𝓞 ρ'` of traces attached to $\rho'$.
--
--   This is Carayol's lemma in the form used in deformation theory: a lift of an absolutely irreducible residual representation is strictly equivalent to one all of whose matrix entries lie in the closed subalgebra topologically generated by the traces. It supplies the descent hypothesis needed for corepresentability of the deformation functor, and is cited by [`GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData`](thm.html#GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData) and by the construction of the Galois representation datum attached to a cusp form.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_TraceAlgebra_descends.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Deformations_TraceAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_Representation_AbsolutelyIrreducible

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing

universe u v

theorem Deformation.TraceAlgebra.descends
    {n : Type} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n] {G : Type u} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G]
    {𝓞 : Type u} [CommRing 𝓞] [IsLocalRing 𝓞] [Finite (IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝓞)]
    {A : Deformation.ProartinianCat 𝓞}
    {ρ₀ : (Deformation.repnFunctor n G 𝓞).obj Deformation.ProartinianCat.residueField}
    [Representation.IsAbsolutelyIrreducible.{u} (Deformation.toRepresentation ρ₀)]
    {ρ' : G →ₜ* GL n A} (hρ' : ρ' ∈ (Deformation.liftFunctor n G 𝓞 ρ₀).obj A) :
    Deformation.TraceAlgebra.Descends ρ' := by sorry
